1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:06,019
Did a woman U.S. officials suspect of spying for China get close to the most powerful man in AI?

2
00:00:06,399 --> 00:00:12,958
Meet Alice Huang, no relation, who ran Megaspeed, a Singapore firm renting out NVIDIA computing power.

3
00:00:13,338 --> 00:00:17,908
Bloomberg estimates it bought at least $4.6 billion of NVIDIA hardware.

4
00:00:18,128 --> 00:00:20,692
Its largest client, reports say: Alibaba.

5
00:00:21,072 --> 00:00:24,865
Renting that power abroad wasn't banned. Shipping chips into China was.

6
00:00:25,085 --> 00:00:26,457
No charges have been filed.

7
00:00:26,837 --> 00:00:33,448
The New York Times reported officials suspect she worked with Chinese intelligence, and had a relationship with Jensen Huang.

8
00:00:33,828 --> 00:00:35,949
Reuters says he called it routine business.

9
00:00:36,329 --> 00:00:37,855
On November 12, he resigned.

10
00:00:38,235 --> 00:00:41,984
China calls the claims groundless. Megaspeed denies wrongdoing.

11
00:00:42,364 --> 00:00:47,589
So, did America's AI tech leak? NVIDIA's board says it has no reason to believe so.

12
00:00:47,969 --> 00:00:48,954
Follow InvisiTech.

